config ZMK_RUNTIME_TAP_DANCE
    bool "Enable runtime-editable tap dance"
    select ZMK_CUSTOM_SETTINGS
    select ZMK_CUSTOM_SETTINGS_ARRAY
    select ZMK_BEHAVIOR_LOCAL_IDS
    help
      Tap-dance slots whose bindings live in custom settings instead of the
      devicetree, so what one tap, two taps or three taps do can be changed
      from Keeb-On! Studio without rebuilding the firmware.

      ZMK's own zmk,behavior-tap-dance is the better choice when the taps
      never need to change: it costs no settings storage. This is for the
      keyboards where they do -- a 30% has to earn every key back.

if ZMK_RUNTIME_TAP_DANCE

config ZMK_RUNTIME_TAP_DANCE_STUDIO_RPC
    bool "Expose tap dance settings to Studio"
    default y
    depends on ZMK_STUDIO
    select ZMK_CUSTOM_SETTINGS_STUDIO_RPC
    help
      Registers this module as a Studio custom subsystem. There is no RPC of
      its own -- the taps are ordinary custom settings -- but a setting whose
      subsystem id matches no registered subsystem is dropped from
      ListSettings, so without this the slots exist on the keyboard and the
      app cannot see them.

config ZMK_RUNTIME_TAP_DANCE_COUNT
    int "Number of tap-dance slots"
    default 4
    range 1 16
    help
      How many independently configurable tap dances exist. A keymap binds
      one by index: `&rtd 0`, `&rtd 1`, and so on. Every slot costs its
      settings entries whether or not it is used, so this is a budget rather
      than a limit to max out.

config ZMK_RUNTIME_TAP_DANCE_MAX_TAPS
    int "Maximum taps per slot"
    default 3
    range 2 5
    help
      The longest tap sequence a slot can hold. Three covers tap / double /
      triple, which is what a 30% layout normally wants; going higher costs
      one stored binding per slot per extra tap and makes the last tap
      slower to reach.

config ZMK_RUNTIME_TAP_DANCE_MAX_HELD
    int "Maximum tap dances in flight at once"
    default 4
    range 1 10
    help
      How many tap dances can be mid-sequence simultaneously. This is about
      fast typing across several tap-dance keys, not about the slot count.

config ZMK_RUNTIME_TAP_DANCE_DEFAULT_TERM_MS
    int "Default tapping term (ms)"
    default 200
    range 50 1000
    help
      How long a slot waits for the next tap before deciding, until someone
      changes it for that slot from the app.

module = ZMK_RUNTIME_TAP_DANCE
module-str = zmk_runtime_tap_dance
source "subsys/logging/Kconfig.template.log_config"

endif # ZMK_RUNTIME_TAP_DANCE
